<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">4 October in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 4 October, from 610 to 1965.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">610</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Heraclius reaches Constantinople to overthrow Phocas</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Heraclius, son of the exarch of Africa, arrived at Constantinople with a fleet from Carthage and toppled the unpopular emperor Phocas. His reign saw triumph over Persia but also the loss of Syria and Egypt to the Arabs.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heraclius">Heraclius</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phocas">Phocas</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1582</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Catholic Europe switches to the Gregorian calendar</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In Italy, Spain, Portugal and Poland, Thursday 4 October 1582 was followed directly by Friday 15 October. Pope Gregory XIII's reform dropped ten days to realign the calendar with the solar year.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1830</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Belgium's provisional government declares independence</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Following the September uprising in Brussels, Belgium's provisional government declared independence from the United Kingdom of the Netherlands. The great powers recognised the new state, and later guaranteed its neutrality.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Kingdom of the Netherlands</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1957</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Soviet Union launches Sputnik 1</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Soviet Union placed Sputnik 1, an 84-kilogram metal sphere, into orbit, the first artificial satellite. Its radio beeps, picked up worldwide, shocked the West and launched the Space Race.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1965</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Paul VI becomes the first pope to visit the United States</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Pope Paul VI flew to New York for a one-day visit, the first by a reigning pope to the United States. He appealed for peace at the United Nations General Assembly and celebrated Mass at Yankee Stadium.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></li></ol>
